  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">UCA Festival Verdad</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The civil war in El Salvador left thousands of people dead or disappeared, and a climate of impunity prevails.  Since the signing of the peace accords, Salvadoran organisations committed to justice and reparation for the victims have worked to keep the historical memory alive and pursued truth.  The UCA Truth Festival began in 1998.  It is an academic, artistic and cultural event that has become a symbol for dignity, truth and breaking down impunity.  The Tribunal of Restorative Justice is a relatively new element of the Truth Festival, beginning in 2009.  The purpose is to insist on the need for justice and an end to impunity to help heal the psychological wounds of the war and build a true peace.  Each year the Tribunal is held in a place that was particularly affected by the civil war.  The first was conducted in the Chapel at the UCA; 2010 - Suchitoto, Cuscutl&#xe1;n;  2011 - Arcatao, Chalatenango;  2012 - Perqu&#xed;n, Moraz&#xe1;n;  2013 - the UCA.  In 2014 it will be held in the community of Santa Marta, in the municipality of Victoria, department of Caba&#xf1;as.</narrative>
  </description>
